---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Newsletter from '../components/Newsletter.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Our Story"
  description="Why Our Health Movement exists: a return to older, gentler knowledge about how to live well, drawing on Ayurveda, Traditional Chinese Medicine and Yoga."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Our Story</p>
      <h1 data-reveal style="--delay: 80ms">A movement back toward<br /><em>older, wiser ways</em></h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lede" data-reveal style="--delay: 160ms">
        We started Our Health Movement for one reason: modern wellness had become loud,
        expensive and complicated, while the wisdom that actually helps people feel well has
        been quietly sitting in ancient traditions all along.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="story-body">
    <div class="wrap-narrow prose" data-reveal-scroll>
      <p class="standfirst">
        For most of human history, health wasn't a product. It was a way of living, woven
        into what you ate, how you moved, when you rested, and your place in the turning of
        the year.
      </p>
      <p>
        Somewhere along the way, we traded a lot of that for convenience. Food arrived
        stripped of its season. Movement became something you scheduled. And a growing haze of
        synthetic fragrances, plastics and additives settled quietly into daily life. We
        gained so much, and mislaid something, too.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Our Health Movement is an attempt to gather it back up.</strong> We look to
        Ayurveda, Traditional Chinese Medicine, Yoga and other enduring traditions, not to
        romanticise the past, but because they hold genuinely useful, time-tested ideas about
        living well. Then we translate them into something you can actually do in a modern
        kitchen.
      </p>
      <p>
        That means seasonal, local eating. Cooking with spices that double as medicine.
        Moving in ways the body was built for, and breathing in ways that settle the nervous
        system. Clearing out the low-level toxic load of everyday life. And sharing all of it
        here, in plain language, free of fads and fear, so you can take what's useful and
        leave the rest.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        The future of feeling well looks a lot like the past: seasonal, unhurried, and deeply
        connected to the natural world.
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Newsletter />
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding-top: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  }
  .page-hero h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-5);
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }
  .page-hero h1 em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--terracotta);
  }
  .page-hero__lede {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 58ch;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .story-body {
    padding-block: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem) clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
  }
  .story-body .prose {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }
  .standfirst {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 60, 'SOFT' 40, 'wght' 370;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .story-body .prose strong {
    color: var(--terracotta-deep);
  }
</style>
